{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeuqQRv2aJkUjgBSJ3iwg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository already has:**\n\n1. **Exception hierarchy**: `ApiException` base class with concrete exceptions `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) and `ConflictException` (409), each tied to an `ErrorCode`\n2. **Centralized error handling**: `GlobalExceptionHandler` maps exceptions to `ApiError` envelope with structure `{error: {code, message, fields}}`\n3. **Error codes**: Closed enum in `ApiError.kt` used for all error responses\n4. **Controller patterns**: Spring `@RestController` with `@PostMapping`, `@GetMapping`, `@RequestMapping`; endpoints return `ResponseEntity` for creates (201) or direct objects for reads (200)\n5. **Repository pattern**: Simple in-memory CRUD interfaces; `findById` returns nullable\n6. **Testing**: MockMvc integration tests checking both status codes and JSON paths; test setup with `@BeforeEach reset()`\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Must add new `ErrorCode` enum value for shipment confirmation conflict (cannot confirm CANCELLED shipment). This is the error contract and must include every possible error the API can return.\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Must add `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the shipment or throws `ResourceNotFoundException`  \n   - Checks if status is CANCELLED and throws `ConflictException` if so\n   - Changes status to CONFIRMED if currently CREATED, otherwise no-op (idempotent)\n   - Saves and returns the shipment\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Must add tests covering:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment → 200 with CONFIRMED status\n   - Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment → 200 (idempotent, unchanged)\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment → 409 with correct error code\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment → 404\n\n**Risks:**\n\n- Idempotency: if the logic doesn't preserve state for already-confirmed shipments, retries fail\n- State validation: CANCELLED must be detected before trying to persist changes\n- Null handling: non-existent shipment must be caught by `findById` returning null\n\nNow entering DESIGN phase.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n**File: ApiError.kt**\nAdd a new error code `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This will be thrown when attempting to confirm a shipment that is in CANCELLED status. The enum now has 6 values instead of 5.\n\n**File: ShipmentController.kt**  \nAdd a new method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` with:\n- `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` annotation\n- Returns `ResponseEntity<Shipment>` with status 200 (default OK)\n- Retrieves shipment via `findById(shipmentId)` or throws `ResourceNotFoundException` with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` code\n- Checks if `shipment.status == ShipmentStatus.CANCELLED` and throws `ConflictException` with new `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` code\n- If status is CREATED, creates a new Shipment with status CONFIRMED\n- If status is already CONFIRMED, no change (idempotent)\n- Saves the shipment (or copy with new status) via repository and returns it\n\n**File: ShipmentControllerTest.kt**\nAdd four new test methods:\n1. `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` — creates S-confirm1 in CREATED, posts to confirm endpoint, expects 200 with CONFIRMED status\n2. `confirm is idempotent for CONFIRMED shipment` — confirms S-confirm2, confirms again, expects 200 with no status change\n3. `rejects confirm of CANCELLED shipment` — directly saves a CANCELLED shipment to repo, posts confirm, expects 409 with error code\n4. `rejects confirm of non-existent shipment` — posts confirm for missing ID, expects 404 with correct error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\nI considered creating a new exception class `ShipmentConfirmationException` for the CANCELLED case, but rejected it because:\n1. `ConflictException` already semantically maps to HTTP 409 \"Conflict\", which fits \"cannot perform action due to current state\"\n2. The existing codebase reuses `ConflictException` for `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` (conflict with existing resource) — two error codes, one exception type is already the pattern\n3. Adding a new exception would require updating `GlobalExceptionHandler` to handle it, increasing scope\n4. The ticket requires \"Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API\" — reusing the existing exception type and adding only an error code maintains consistency\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Flow |\n|------|------|\n| Confirm CREATED shipment | GET from repo by ID → check not CANCELLED → copy to new Shipment(status=CONFIRMED) → save → return 200 |\n| Confirm already CONFIRMED | GET from repo by ID → check not CANCELLED → no change needed → return 200 (unchanged) |\n| Confirm CANCELLED shipment | GET from repo by ID → throw ConflictException(\"SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\", msg) → GlobalExceptionHandler maps to 409 |\n| Confirm non-existent | GET from repo returns null → throw ResourceNotFoundException(\"SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\", msg) → maps to 404 |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nEach test follows the same pattern:\n1. Create a shipment (or seed the repo directly for CANCELLED case) via createShipment helper or direct save\n2. POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm\n3. Assert status code and body structure (for errors, check `$.error.code`)\n\nThis covers all four terminal cases named in the ticket: success, idempotent success, CANCELLED conflict, missing 404.\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll write the code."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1991,"cache_read_input_tokens":19401,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1991},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"deededcb-69e4-4e5b-be6b-11da0c72e8a6","uuid":"4da3be2e-35a1-4673-8f1a-4d74213285bb","timestamp":"2026-09-10T13:27:00.259Z","request_id":"req_011CeuqQRC7r3fNgiWpvwyaF"}
